{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "cz-tapes — five czsynth tracks and a dusty kit, at 68bpm in C minor.",
    "",
    "czsynth is an emulation of the Casio CZ-101 (1984), the phase-distortion",
    "synthesizer behind most of what people mean by 'the Boards of Canada",
    "sound'. There is no filter in it. One cosine table is read with a phase",
    "that has been bent by a piecewise-linear function, so a period still takes",
    "exactly one period but is traversed unevenly — and the DCW envelope moves",
    "how hard it is bent. That sounds uncannily like a filter opening while",
    "being nothing of the sort.",
    "",
    "The 28 presets are real patches, decoded from Casio sysex dumps — one",
    "folder per record. /keys preset=random rolls a different one.",
    "",
    "  keys    turquoise-hexagon-sun-epiano   authored chord stabs",
    "  flute   orangey-flute                  authored melody",
    "  pad     twoism-pulse-pad               <- wash (chorale)",
    "  bells   zander-two-bells               <- sparkle (randomnotes)",
    "  bass    a03-bass                       authored root notes",
    "  kick/kit  percsampler                  <- grid (euclidpercs)",
    "",
    "Every track is one preset plus seven modifier params on top of it. The one",
    "that matters is dcw — this synth's filter knob:",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /keys                      the preset, its waveform and both envelopes",
    "  /keys dcw=0 8b             close it right down; every waveform is a sine",
    "  /keys dcw=1 8b             and back",
    "  /keys dcw=2                past where the hardware's envelope could reach",
    "  /keys wave=square          override the waveform, preset untouched",
    "  /keys wave=reso1           the 'resonant' wave — see the note below",
    "  /keys wave=preset          give it back",
    "  /keys env_time=4 8b        stretch every envelope; an epiano becomes a pad",
    "  /keys preset=oirectine-epiano   a combination wave, with a sub-octave",
    "  /bells lines=1             drop the line detuned two octaves up",
    "  /flute vib_depth=60 8b     lean on the vibrato",
    "  /pad detune=80 16b         drag the two lines apart",
    "  /bass octave=0             out of the basement",
    "  /keys random               roll every param at once",
    "  /harmony root=58           move it all to Bb",
    "",
    "Two things behave unlike the rest of the engine, both on purpose:",
    "",
    "A preset is selected by an option, and the other four options each take",
    "the sentinel 'preset', meaning 'whatever the tone says'. So choosing a new",
    "preset never clobbers an override, and an override never has to be",
    "re-applied. Set one back to 'preset' to return it.",
    "",
    "And on the three resonant waveforms — reso1/reso2/reso3 — dcw moves a",
    "frequency, not a brightness. Those three are not phase distortion at all:",
    "they are an inner sine hard-synced to the note and multiplied by a",
    "per-cycle window, and dcw sets how many cycles fit in a period. Casio",
    "named them after the window shape, which has confused people for forty",
    "years.",
    "",
    "The effects follow the routing notes that came with the patches: a plate",
    "on the verb bus (the Midiverb everything went through), a quarter-note",
    "echo, a triplet delay with no feedback on the bells, a highs boost on the",
    "keys and a low tilt on the bass. Width is all downstream — czsynth renders",
    "mono, because the CZ-101 has one output and these records kept summing it.",
    "",
    "  warble -> keys.dcw      the epiano brightens and dulls over ~22 seconds",
    "  drift  -> pad.detune    the pad slowly pulls itself out of tune",
    "",
    "A czsynth param is read once per note, not continuously — so a ramp or a",
    "patch on dcw arrives note by note. Held notes keep the brightness they",
    "started with, which is exactly how the hardware behaves."
  ],
